[thin] Nominal structural-section threshold reading. These exact anchors lie on the source-defined Ø18/Ø12 support rings or 3.00 mm upright webs. The source-to-canonical STEP Boolean identity is exact; the current STL reports 2.999..3.000 mm at its faceted circular surfaces and nominal 3 mm planes. This explains tessellation/strict-threshold readings at the specified nominal wall, without accepting a thinner authored web. The material-thickness ranking remains visible.
alternatives: Increasing the native dimensions to conceal sub-micron or one-micron mesh readings changes the nominal ring or web and its clearances. Finer tessellation changes mesh size and chord error, not the source section. An actually smaller native section would require a source correction.
