[ceiling] Build-direction classification mismatch. This frame prints on its broad fore Y face, with source +Y rotated to build +Z; it does not print in its installed source-Z direction. Each anchored face is vertical in that prescribed pose. The current-STL Y-normal audit finds zero ceiling, ledge, slope or sliver findings. The unmodified complete canonical lint retains all of these installed-Z findings, separately from the pose audit; neither reading qualifies printed fit or strength.
alternatives: Printing the frame upright in its installed Z pose makes these overhang classifications relevant. Sloping or filling these vertical side profiles in the prescribed flat pose changes the ring openings and bridge geometry to address the wrong build direction. The manual linter currently accepts only source-Z sign, so the Y pose is documented explicitly.
